# Written by thinkpad-power's install.sh when FINGERPRINT_WAKE=on. The vendor
# and product ids are filled in from the reader found on this machine.
#
# The fingerprint reader loses power in S3 and re-enumerates on resume. The
# lock screen starts its PAM fingerprint session before that finishes, gets
# "device was disconnected", and retries — four times in 900 ms on this
# machine before the fourth one caught a live device. Marking the reader as
# wake-capable asks the platform to keep its port powered through suspend, so
# there is nothing to re-enumerate.
#
# This costs sleep power: a powered USB port is the opposite of what the rest
# of this tool is for. It is a knob, not a default. Turn it off by setting
# FINGERPRINT_WAKE=off in /etc/thinkpad-power.conf and re-running install.sh.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="@VID@", ATTR{idProduct}=="@PID@", ATTR{power/wakeup}="enabled"
